  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Socioeconomic Inclusion Efforts for Refugees from Ukraine in Selected European Union (EU) Member States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the IOM 2023 Appeal for Ukraine and Neighbouring Countries and the inter-agency 2023 Refugee Response Plan (RRP) for the Ukraine Situation as well as in one with planning exercises around the 2024 RRP, the proposed project aims to enable IOM and its partners to continue responding to persisting and growing humanitarian needs, and reduce and mitigate underlying vulnerabilities and risk by providing lifesaving assistance and protection support to the most vulnerable people affected by the war in Ukraine. Simultaneously, IOM will pivot existing capacities to work for longer-term solutions for refugees from Ukraine, with a focus on their most urgent needs to achieve stability, including housing and accommodation, health (including mental health and psychosocial support) and livelihood interventions. IOM will look at these sectors from a social inclusion point of view and will focus on supporting beneficiaries overcoming barriers to access social and economic participation in host countries to enable self-reliance. Interventions are fully aligned with two priorities of the Rapid Response Fund (RRF), namely 1) strengthening infrastructure for migrants with a focus on shelter and accommodation; and 2) supporting integration measures.</narrative>
  </description>
